Beside our T=4 MAXDIM=64 logic-only (1,396,966.00): ours is 3.66x. Note the shape of the
difference, not just its size -- Gemmini's logic is 38.3% non-combinational against our
80.1%, so ours is flop-heavy where theirs is gate-heavy, and 60.2% of ours sits in four
AXI adapters. Whether Gemmini's StreamReader/StreamWriter/XactTracker carry comparable
adapter mass is the open question and needs its hierarchy report, which this run can
still supply from its mapped database.
